  "term": "aortic arch syndrome",
  "definition": "Aortic arch syndrome is a group of disorders caused by problems in the arteries that branch from the aorta’s arch area. Reduced or abnormal blood flow to the head, neck, or arm can lead to neurological problems and weakness in an arm.",
